ake sure that  we deliver to the european uh citizens  but that we also  deliver to the world  oh excuse me i have not answered  your question on the on the vaccines in  italy  you were asking that too here the  company has uh  um has made clear that of the  um 29 million doses 13 million doses  are for covax and 16 million doses  are for european member states  and indeed we for us is important  that vaccines are being delivered to  to kovacs kovacs is the main pillar to  make sure that law and middle-income  countries have access to vaccines  the drug substance that has been used  for fill and finish in the italian  production site came from south korea  and china and um this was  and is the usual way to um work on  producing the vaccines for coverage  maybe just a few words there is a very  strong consensus among the member states  first  uh we want to guarantee the supply  chains and we want an open economy  but at the same time we want more  transparency and this  the goal with this mechanism put on the  table by the by the commission  and we want to make sure that the the  contracts  are fulfilled and indeed there are some  concerns serious concerns  with regard to this one company and we  hope that with the support of this  tool this instrument it will be possible  to to increase  not only the production and the delivery  and then finally another important part  a few  weeks ago in a newsletter i've tried to  explain  that europe is a major producer  of vaccines we export a lot of vaccines  and we have all the tools in order to  in order to succeed and to increase the  production  and to deliver more doses in the next  week  thank you mr president we have uh angela  maro from huffington post  angela you have the floor  angela there you are  could you please unmute  hello we can't hear you  we'll take another question  maria mariapsara you are next  from opentv maria hello can you hear me  can you see me maybe  we can hear you and see you okay so  two questions on turkey if i may you  mentioned migration  modernizing custom union two things that  turkey has been asking for a long time  could you say that this is the beginning  of the new era between  for the relationship between the eu and  turkey  and the second question you are  considering of going  to turkey that's what you said after the  teleconference with  president erdogan will this trip be  before  june do you know already thanks  to two points first point i can only  repeat a twist this decision that we  that we took today we have a clear  framework and  we hope we really hope it will be  possible to improve the relationship  with turkey but at the same time  i repeat that for us it's important that  turkey  keep a positive behavior a moderate  behavior and we hope that the dialogue  will be  fruitful but we remain we remain  cautious and remain careful and indeed  we are in contact with  the turkish authorities in order to pay  a visit probably in april  to turkey well what  the migration topic is concerned  um we think the commission was mandated  today  or invited by the council to work on  that as you know  there is the eu uh turkey statement  since  2016 first of all the  return and resettlement mechanism  has to be put in place again and  secondly indeed  um so far the six billion in this  um eu turkey statement have been  contracted by now  four billion have been dispersed the  other projects are still ongoing  we have the uh financial contribution  for bridging  time frame till the end of 2021  it is important we think to  continue to engage in this field for  very simple reason  turkey is hosting um 3.6  million syrian refugees and  there's a major contribution from the  european union  to support those syrian refugees beat  schooling for the  children 2 million children are  in school during that time have been in  school during that time  be it support for for example medical  medical appointments but also be  investment  in the infrastructure without any doubt  turkey is shouldering  the major the lion's share of the burden  but we think  it is important to keep on going  with the support in this humanitarian  cause  concerning the syrian refugees in turkey  and the discussion  and negotiations will go on how to  proceed  with this eu turkey statement this is  one of the major topics we will  certainly discuss  thank you we'll take a question from  politico david  hersenhorten david you're next thanks  very much brent  a question for each president if i can  president michelle i wonder if you could  talk to us about  uh your conversation with president  biden and specifically if he'd made any  offer  to send vaccines at some point to the eu  perhaps even to austria  to help you out in various ways and for  president fender line  on the export control mechanism i wonder  if how you would react to folks who say  as this pandemic era leads to a boom in  the vaccine industry will this  discourage  companies from setting up in the eu  because they see these sorts of  bureaucratic restrictions and also given  the numbers you presented  should your friend boris johnson also  come forward with his numbers of exports  of vaccines around the world thank you  both  in fact i i would like to repeat again  that uh  europe exports a lot of doses everywhere  in the in the world and the top priority  is to increase  the production of vaccines and literally  are convinced that it's important to  have a very strong cooperation  with the united states when it when it  comes to distraction  of the supply chain that is why the  commission and especially  thierry bertone and the task force they  are in touch  with the american administration in  order to guarantee  the supply chains and the certainty for  us in europe that you are able  in the next weeks and months to produce  more doses  and we cooperate also with the united  states and with other  countries in the world when it comes to  the kovacs facility  you know that uh we played a very  important role the european union  union you know to launch this initiative  because  with joe biden and we repeat it this uh  conviction we will not be safe until  everyone is safe and that's why it's key  to property to progress  it's key to vaccinate to vaccinate and  to speed up  the vaccinations campaign so on your  question  i think that it was good  to introduce the expert authorization  mechanism  indeed to create transparency  because that proves that the european  union is the most  open reliably exporting  region in the world the united states  have their executive order  i have no knowledge so far of uk exports  perhaps i'm mistaken  and waiting for that transparency  and the same goes for many other regions  in the world  so if only or only the export  authorization mechanism created the  transparency  to show how much the european  region is doing when it comes to  producing and exporting vaccines to the  world that's the first point  where i think it's encouraging for the  companies  because their their achievements are  being honored by that the second point  is  that indeed we have a strong  interest in expanding  the vaccine production in the european  union to be prepared  for the next years to be prepared  for variants to come to be prepared  for the time where we will at a certain  point in time  have to reboost uh the immunity um  against covet or covet variants  in the european union so our interest is  to intensify the cooperation with  the reliable companies the companies  that have proven  that they can scale up and that they  honor their contracts  over the next years also to invest  in that because we think in an era of  pandemic it's the right way to go  thank you madam president this concludes  our press conference of this evening  thank you all for joining  and see you soon  [Music]  you
 

